 ### 9\. Brainstorming Questions

 Before moving to the design/development phase, the team should decide:

 - Who is the primary target user?
- Will ComicCraft create **scripts only**, or complete visual comics?
- Will users be able to upload their own character references?
- What comic styles should initially be supported?
- Should users control story length and complexity?
- How much control should users have over individual panels?
- Should the system remember characters across chapters?
- What export formats should be supported?
- Which Gemini model capabilities will be used for text, multimodal understanding, and image-related workflows?

 ### 10\. Initial Project Vision

 > **ComicCraft aims to make comic creation accessible by transforming a user's simple idea into an editable, structured comic through AI-assisted storytelling, character development, scene planning, dialogue generation, and panel design.**

 This gives the project a clear **Brainstorming & Ideation Phase** foundation before moving into requirements, UI/UX design, system architecture, and implementation.Brainstorming & Ideation Phase
